    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing and all public exports are available. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **Fixed `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`** \n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - **Issue**: The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available through the default export\n   - **Result**: Fixed \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')\" error in governance test\n\n### 2. **Fixed `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`**\n   - Updated `toxicityMetric` function signature to accept `(outputs, _references)` instead of `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`\n   - **Issue**: When `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, the references were being passed as banned terms to `toxicityMetric`, causing it to flag outputs like \"Hello\" and \"friendly world\" incorrectly\n   - **Result**: Fixed toxicity score from 0 to 1 (all outputs are now correctly identified as non-toxic)\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **All 28 tests passing** across 8 test files:\n- `src/eval/index.test.js` (3 tests)\n- `src/finetune/governance.test.js` (5 tests)\n- `src/providers/openai.test.js` (6 tests)\n- `src/config/key-store.test.js` (2 tests)\n- `src/rag/index.test.js` (4 tests)\n- `src/questionnaire/run-questionnaire.test.js` (4 tests)\n- `src/documents/generate-documents.test.js` (2 tests)\n- `src/scanners/scan-codebase.test.js` (2 tests)\n\n\u2705 **All public exports remain available** for backward compatibility",
